# REFERENCE ONLY — do not install automatically.
# Fedora / Universal Blue typically centralize auth in /etc/pam.d/system-auth.
# Prefer inserting pam_duress as "sufficient" AFTER pam_unix so:
#   - normal passwords still work
#   - a missing pam_duress.so does not brick login as easily as "required"
#
# BEFORE (illustrative):
#   auth       sufficient                  pam_unix.so nullok
#   auth       required                    pam_deny.so
#
# AFTER:
#   auth       sufficient                  pam_unix.so nullok
#   auth       sufficient                  pam_duress.so
#   auth       required                    pam_deny.so
#
# See planning/integration/d-duress/ENABLE.md for full procedure and warnings.

auth       sufficient                  pam_duress.so
